  "answer": "To add middleware to a FastAPI application, you can use the `app.add_middleware()` method. This method allows you to integrate ASGI middlewares into your FastAPI application. Here is an example of how to use it:\n\n```Python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI\nfrom unicorn import UnicornMiddleware\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\napp.add_middleware(UnicornMiddleware, some_config=\"rainbow\")\n```\n\nThis example uses the `UnicornMiddleware` middleware, which is a class that expects to receive an ASGI app as the first argument. FastAPI provides a simpler way to add middleware that ensures server errors and custom exception handlers work properly.",
